        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SCchAOsyZcud_EP7V0Vg-113" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=0" value="&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px;&quot;&gt;The browser requests the application&#39;s frontend files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) and hotel images through Amazon CloudFront, which is protected by AWS WAF. CloudFront retrieves the frontend assets from the private S3 Frontend bucket and the hotel images from the private Hotel Images bucket using Origin Access Control (OAC), ensuring that both buckets remain inaccessible from the public Internet.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="76" width="1177" x="487.5" y="1357" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SCchAOsyZcud_EP7V0Vg-114" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;For an authenticated application request, the browser sends an HTTPS request containing the JWT in the Authorization header. CloudFront forwards dynamic API requests through a CloudFront VPC Origin to the internal Application Load Balancer, keeping the application backend private and inaccessible directly from the Internet.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="69" width="1105" x="487.5" y="1403.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SCchAOsyZcud_EP7V0Vg-115" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="The internal Application Load Balancer evaluates the request path and routes the traffic to the corresponding ECS target group: &lt;code&gt;/search&lt;/code&gt; to the Search Service, &lt;code&gt;/reservation&lt;/code&gt; to the Reservation/Admin Service, and &lt;code&gt;/analytics&lt;/code&gt; to the Metabase Service." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="840" x="480" y="1471" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SCchAOsyZcud_EP7V0Vg-116" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;p&gt;Before an ECS Fargate task can process the request, it accesses required AWS services privately without using a NAT Gateway. ECR Interface Endpoints together with the S3 Gateway Endpoint allow container images to be pulled from Amazon ECR, Secrets Manager provides application credentials, and the CloudWatch Logs Interface Endpoint allows application logs to be sent privately to CloudWatch.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="67" width="1260" x="480" y="1510" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="SCchAOsyZcud_EP7V0Vg-117" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;p&gt;Depending on the request path, the ALB routes the request to the appropriate ECS service. The Search Service queries Amazon OpenSearch to retrieve hotel availability, the Reservation/Admin Service manages reservations and hotel inventory, and the Metabase Service provides the analytics interface. Protected application APIs validate Cognito JWTs in the backend using &lt;code&gt;aws-jwt-verify&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="1060" x="486" y="1567" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
